{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>This is the land that shall fall to you as an inheritance.</b> It shall fall to you by lot before you conquer all of it, for the language of \"falling\" is fitting for a lot, as in וְעַל לְבוּשִׁי יַפִּילוּ גוֹרָל (Psalms 22:19), and likewise הִפִּיל פּוּר הוּא הַגּוֹרָל (Esther 3:7). And it says \"this,\" because what they conquered outside the land did not require division by lot; accordingly Moses divided the land of Sihon and Og without a lot, as is apparent in the book of Joshua. This is because the land of Sihon and Og does not possess the sanctity of the land of Israel, as it says וְאַךְ אִם טְמֵאָה אֶרֶץ אֲחֻזַּתְכֶם (Joshua 22:19), and it was not fit for a lot, whose nature is through the Holy Spirit."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:41:41.786818231Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}